# Sellers and buyers on a marketplace, with the marketplace-and-payouts pack
# acting. A seller is a store (the tenant) owned by an account; a sale is a
# payment.succeeded with the store as tenant_id and the buyer as actor_id.
# Store 1 opened two days ago and asks for a payout for orders not delivered
# yet: held for 7 days. Store 2 is old but changed its payout destination the
# day before, and asks again the next day. Store 3 is a young store whose
# sales jumped. Store 4 has a high refund rate, store 5 a high dispute rate.
# Six buyer accounts on one device buy from one store and use one promo code;
# one buyer owns the store it buys from. A well-established store gets its
# payout without friction.
# packs: marketplace-and-payouts
# enforce
# Store 1: new store, payout before delivery
